vsock/virtio: 256 KiB packets and receive buffers

The driver posts 4 KiB receive buffers, so a stream from the host arrives
as sixteen packets per 64 KiB, each with a header, a completion and a
copy of its own; measured on the M5 the guest's core was the bound at
6.5 Gbit/s. A buffer the size of the largest packet the transport sends
(VIRTIO_VSOCK_MAX_PKT_BUF_SIZE) takes the whole packet at once. The
allocation is order-4, which the guest has after its idle compaction.

--- a/include/linux/virtio_vsock.h
+++ b/include/linux/virtio_vsock.h
@@ -135,9 +135,9 @@
  * rounding up to the next page order and also means that we
  * don't leave higher-order pages sitting around in the RX queue.
  */
-#define VIRTIO_VSOCK_DEFAULT_RX_BUF_SIZE	SKB_WITH_OVERHEAD(1024 * 4)
+#define VIRTIO_VSOCK_DEFAULT_RX_BUF_SIZE	SKB_WITH_OVERHEAD(1024 * 256)
 #define VIRTIO_VSOCK_MAX_BUF_SIZE		0xFFFFFFFFUL
-#define VIRTIO_VSOCK_MAX_PKT_BUF_SIZE		(1024 * 64)
+#define VIRTIO_VSOCK_MAX_PKT_BUF_SIZE		(1024 * 256)
 
